1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,046
Meet Mini Film Director: the idea of a local phone app that helps solo
creators plan, perform, and shape their content.

2
00:00:07,146 --> 00:00:14,574
Start with your objective. Here, we want a twenty-second jacket
reveal, with texture, a walk, and a confident final pose.

3
00:00:14,674 --> 00:00:23,384
Review the reference shots, then choose what to borrow: timing,
angles, or posing. This example is invented; no Instagram reel was
downloaded.

4
00:00:23,484 --> 00:00:30,403
Use as my shot plan asks for confirmation. Your objective, opening
line, and existing takes stay with your project.

5
00:00:30,503 --> 00:00:36,630
The result is five editable shots. Adjust any cue or duration.
Applying a plan does not begin recording.

6
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:42,389
Press Start this shoot. The director gives one posing cue at a time.
Spoken guidance is optional.

7
00:00:42,489 --> 00:00:47,649
Then comes the countdown. Three, two, one. You always have a Stop
control.

8
00:00:47,749 --> 00:00:53,835
Action begins a timed sample take. In this web demo, the image is an
illustration, not a live camera.

9
00:00:53,935 --> 00:00:58,035
Cut saves the sample draft, then the sequence moves to the next shot.

10
00:00:58,135 --> 00:01:03,937
When the shoot finishes, your takes appear in Edit. Review the
sequence, then trim or reorder clips.

11
00:01:04,037 --> 00:01:11,290
Captions, sound direction, and the cover remain editable. These web
captions are samples, rather than a transcription result.

12
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:18,309
Name your film and save it explicitly. The project keeps your brief,
shots, captions, and edit decisions together.

13
00:01:18,409 --> 00:01:26,227
Projects holds your saved films in this browser. Reopen one, or
download its JSON backup. This website does not export a video.

14
00:01:26,327 --> 00:01:35,461
The local-phone vision combines Qwen with small speech models.
Separate Android CPU inference has been tested; the complete speech
and vision loop still needs validation.

15
00:01:35,561 --> 00:01:42,422
Mini Film Director. A pre-event design prototype, showing how a solo
creator could move from an idea to a reviewed film.
